:: Church encounter - basement expecting [bg-basement]
<h1 class="ptitle">BASEMENT</h1>
<br /><br />
/* A kind nun looks after a slave who is expecting (base policy: nuns may include slaves). Late in the pregnancy she helps her get around too. Feral nuns too. */
<<set _ce = setup.churchEncounters>>
<<set _fx = setup.nurseryEncounters>>
<<set _cast = _ce.cast()>>
<<if !_cast>>
	<<goto 'Basement'>>
<<else>>
<<set _nun = _cast.nun, _slave = _cast.slave>>
<<set _feral = _ce.isFeral(_nun)>>
<<set _nunName = setup.displayName(_nun), _sName = setup.displayName(_slave)>>
<<set _nHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_nun), _nHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_nun), _nHim = setup.pronounceWho(_nun)>>
<<set _sHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_slave), _sHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_slave), _sHim = setup.pronounceWho(_slave)>>
<<set _sMc = setup.npc.mcName(_slave), _nMc = setup.npc.mcName(_nun)>>
<<set _heavy = (_slave.pregnancy ?? 0) >= _ce.HEAVY_FROM>>
<<set _babyIsMc = _slave.pregnancy_father === 'mc'>>

<<if _heavy>>
	<<=_sName>> is trying to get up from the cot in <<=_sHis>> cell, which at this stage of <<=_sHis>> pregnancy is a project in several stages. <<=_nunName>> is already at <<=_sHis>> side, one arm around <<=_sHis>> back and the other braced under <<=_sHis>> elbow, taking most of <<=_sHis>> weight as <<=_sHe>> rocks forward onto <<=_sHis>> feet.
<<else>>
	<<=_sName>> is propped up on <<=_sHis>> cot with <<=_sHis>> feet up on a rolled blanket, one hand resting on the curve of <<=_sHis>> belly. <<=_nunName>> has brought a pillow down from upstairs and is fussing with it behind <<=_sHis>> back, plumping it when it doesn't need plumping.
<</if>>
<br /><br />
<<if _feral>>
	<<if _heavy>>
		<<sayFeral _nun>>keeps a steady hold on <<=_sName>> until <<=_sHe>> is upright and balanced, then walks beside <<=_sHim>> step for step out of the cell, shoulder pressed to <<=_sHis>> side, ready to catch<</sayFeral>>
	<<else>>
		<<sayFeral _nun>>sets a cup of water by the cot, nudges it closer when <<=_sName>> doesn't reach for it right away, and then lays <<=_nHis>> head very gently against <<=_sHis>> belly, listening<</sayFeral>>
	<</if>>
	<br />
	<<sayNpc _slave>>
		<<=ucfirst(_sMc)>>, <<=_nHe>> comes down every day now. <<=ucfirst(_nHe)>> doesn't let me do a thing for myself. I think <<=_nHe>> knows what I need before I do.
	<</sayNpc>>
<<else>>
	<<sayNpc _nun>>
		<<if _heavy>>
			Slowly. Lean on me, that's what I'm here for. There's no prize for doing it alone.
		<<else>>
			Water first, then you can have the tea. And tell me if your back starts aching again. These cots are hard enough without a baby to carry.
		<</if>>
	<</sayNpc>>
	<br />
	<<sayNpc _slave>>
		<<=ucfirst(_sMc)>>. <<=ucfirst(_nHe)>> comes down here every day now. <<=ucfirst(_nHe)>> won't let me do a thing for myself.
	<</sayNpc>>
	<br />
	<<sayNpc _nun>>
		The holy texts call a new life the first gift of the divine, <<=_nMc>>, and they don't say anything about which side of a door it's carried on. The least I can do is fetch the water for the one carrying the gift.
	<</sayNpc>>
<</if>>
<br />

<div id="ce_choices">
	<<link 'Lend a hand (Uses 30 minutes)'>>
		<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
			<<addmins 30>>
			<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _slave, 'happy', 2, 4)>>
			<<run _fx.change(_slave, 'relationship', 2, 4)>>
			<<run _fx.change(_nun, 'happy', 1, 2)>>
			<<run _fx.change(_nun, 'relationship', 1, 2)>>
			<<run _ce.changePlayer('goodwill', 2)>>
			<<if _heavy>>
				You take <<=_sName>>'s other arm, and between you and <<=_nunName>> <<=_sHe>> makes a slow lap of the basement, past the other cells and back. You fetch a stool when <<=_sHe>> needs to rest, rub the small of <<=_sHis>> back while <<=_sHe>> gets <<=_sHis>> breath back, and walk <<=_sHim>> home to <<=_sHis>> cot again at whatever pace <<=_sHe>> likes.
			<<else>>
				You roll up your sleeves. You refill the water, rub <<=_sName>>'s swollen feet while <<=_nunName>> brews the tea on the stove upstairs, and bring down a second blanket from storage so <<=_sHe>> won't be cold in the night.
			<</if>>
			<br /><br />
			<<sayNpc _slave>>
				<<if _babyIsMc>>
					I like seeing you like this, <<=_sMc>>. Taking care of the both of us.
				<<else>>
					Thank you, <<=_sMc>>. I didn't think anyone would look after me like this down here.
				<</if>>
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			<<if _feral>>
				<<sayFeral _nun>>watches you work with <<=_nHis>> head tilted, then copies you, rubbing <<=_sName>>'s other foot with exactly the same careful motion<</sayFeral>>
			<<else>>
				<<sayNpc _nun>>
					This is what the church is for, <<=_nMc>>. Not the altar or the candles. This, wherever it's needed.
				<</sayNpc>>
			<</if>>
			<br />
			[[Continue|Basement]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	<<link 'Leave them be'>>
		<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
			You leave <<=_sName>> in <<=_nunName>>'s care. <<=ucfirst(_sHe)>> couldn't be in better hands.
			<br /><br />
			[[Continue|Basement]]
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
</div>
<</if>>
